arospkg 0.3.2 -- AROS x86_64 ABIv11
==================================

This patch updates apkg's download progress. PkgManager is the unchanged
0.3.1 binary. Other CPU/ABI builds remain available in release 0.3.1.

INSTALL

Close PkgManager and finish running apkg commands before updating.
Keep SYS:Packages: it contains installed applications and their records.

  UnZip arospkg-0.3.2.x86_64-aros-v11.zip
  CD arospkg-0.3.2.x86_64-aros-v11
  Copy apkg C:
  apkg --version
  apkg update

Keep this drawer somewhere permanent if using the graphical interface:

  Run PkgManager

No compiler or separate TLS libraries are required. You need an x86_64
ABIv11 system, crt.library and stdlib.library; PkgManager also needs Zune
(muimaster.library). Downloads need networking and the certificate bundle
ENV:SYS/Certificates/ca-bundle.crt.

USE

  apkg search soliton
  apkg show soliton
  apkg install soliton

Open SYS:Packages/soliton in Wanderer and launch the program inside.
PkgManager offers the same catalogue and Install/Remove operations.
Use apkg list to see installed packages, apkg verify soliton to check one,
and apkg remove soliton to remove it while retaining locally changed and
user-created files. For a different package root pass --root Work:Packages
to both front ends consistently.

WHAT CHANGED

Download progress uses complete milestone lines every 10%, rather than
redrawing a bar that can leave fragments after a window is narrowed.
In Limpet, each new line fits the current width with one column spare;
narrow windows show fewer details. Success, error and cancellation start
on separate lines. --plain, JSON and redirected output are unchanged.
Colours, show/search layout and package operations remain as before.

CHECKS AND LIMITS

The progress change was exercised on AROS One 1.3 under QEMU with Limpet
rc5: both themes, narrowing, multiple updates, widening, completion and
cancellation. The host suite passed. The final apkg rebuild changes the
version identification from the guest-tested development build to 0.3.2;
that final rebuild was not separately run in the guest.
PkgManager is byte-identical to the published 0.3.1 program.

TLS uses Mbed TLS with jitterentropy on this target. The entropy assessment
remains limited to the previously tested QEMU configuration; the restart
series is incomplete. This update makes no new security-validation claim.

BUILD.txt records source revisions and program SHA-256 hashes.
SHA256SUMS on the release page checks the downloadable archive.
Licences are in LICENSE and licenses/. ARexx examples are in Examples/ARexx/.

